    'DoubaoSeedEvolving0827(Max)V1-TasksAssignedByOpus5': "Offline native WebGL2 with an HDR fallback, scene 4× MSAA, reciprocal ring shadows, density-based atmosphere, moving belts, bloom and final ACES. JPL rates, Kepler motion and epochs are implemented. All eight satellites retain task-compliance credit for the prescribed local +Z/basis algorithm, with actual directed angles preserved. Equal-mean-anomaly sampling of Halley into only 384 segments leaves a maximum compressed-space path error of 8.1227 versus a .16 nucleus radius, so path fit is partial. The actual model matrix reverses ordinary Earth surface rotation, and every satellite is illuminated from its parent rather than the Sun; together these reduce data credit. The sunward ion tail retains a separate integrity deduction. Spin still advances while paused and the .5 overview zoom floor lies inside the radius-4.6 Sun. After zoom settled within 2% of its target, only 3 of 12 default-speed Io samples remained on screen, with repeated negative depth; follow is partial. Paused JD stayed fixed while Earth spin advanced from .3776 to 2.01797.",
