    'Opus5Ultra-WebGL2': 'All eight features, bidirectional ring shadows, and the complete interaction set are present. It remains one of the three benchmark entries whose table cells keep the gold label while exposing the score on hover.',
    'Opus5Ultra-TasksAssignedByOpus5': "The offline native WebGL2 model implements JPL secular/Keplerian planetary orbits, a return-calibrated Halley orbit, bidirectional ring shadows, moving small bodies, HDR/Bloom/ACES and atmospheric shells. Directed moon normals validate only Triton: its negative period and actual right-handed frame together give 156.9°. The Moon and six other equatorial moons move in the wrong direction. Orbit ribbons sample eccentric anomaly from the same curves. Retrograde geometric poles are combined with negative spin periods, and lunar surface rotation is not correctly synchronized; these receive a modest data deduction. Drag, focus and continuous follow work, but the 0.02 zoom minimum enters bodies and Now resets only the date, so full-state reset is absent.",
