    'GLM5.3(Max)V2-TasksAssignedByOpus5': "Offline native WebGL2 implements JPL rates, Kepler motion, radial compression, planetary pole models, reciprocal ring shadows, density atmosphere, moving belts, bloom followed by ACES, HDR and MSAA. No fatal error is inferred merely from LINEAR in a GL0 resolve path. Six of eight satellites retain task-compliance credit for the prescribed local +Z algorithm. Triton independently changes the required negative period to positive, producing a prograde 23.1° plane. Newly confirmed: Charon’s display distance remains zero and it coincides with Pluto, so it does not count. Orbit buffers duplicate every sample but POINTS draws only n of 2n vertices, omitting the second half of every path. Halley has a genuine orbit, period and active double tail, retaining its three points; however no nucleus or coma is drawn beyond 6.5AU, reducing integrity. No other independent data fault is established; prompt-inherent spin and June/July conflicts are exempt. The .05 zoom floor remains unsafe; drag, focus, exact following, pause, Now and reverse are retained.",
    'Opus_4_8_Max': "Bundled Three.js uses focused ellipses, Newton Kepler solving, real angular elements and J2000 mean longitude minus perihelion longitude, with matching paths. Semimajor axes are arbitrary display distances rather than real ratios, giving partial element credit. All eight moons have random ecliptic inclinations, move opposite the reflected planet orbits and omit two pi from their periods; they are invalid without repeated data deductions. Rings lack physical shadows. The moving belt, Bloom/OutputPass ACES work and atmospheres are Fresnel glows. The x,z,y reflection is not matched by spin-axis conventions, with additional signed-axis double flips for Venus/Uranus. Drag, safe zoom, focus and displacement follow work. Pause stops planet/moon motion while Sun/cloud animation continues; reset restores the camera rather than the initial date. Half-float postprocessing has no fallback or scene MSAA.",
