    'Grok4.6(xhigh)V1': "Ten planets/dwarfs and Halley use approximate real elements, Kepler solving and matching paths, but all start at perihelion at simulation zero without an epoch. Halley’s eccentric retrograde orbit is implemented. Of twelve moons, the independent5.15-degree Moon with its correct period is valid. The other eleven apply equatorial inclinations directly in the ecliptic frame; Triton also double-flips negative period and retrograde inclination. They are invalid, without repeated data deductions. The moving belt, Bloom/OutputPass ACES work; unlit MeshBasic rings have no physical shadows and atmospheres are rims. Venus/Uranus/Pluto double-flip tilted axes and negative spins. Focus/follow mainly steer the target and move the camera only when distant; minimum distance4 is inside the Sun’s radius4.6. Pause leaves Sun/wind motion running and reset restores the camera. Half-float postprocessing has no fallback or scene MSAA.",
