    'DeepSeek_V4_Pro_high-2': "Eight planets use approximate periods on circular paths with inclinations and random phase, without Keplerian timing or epoch. Static path lines omit the complete phase-dependent Euler transform. A three-coordinate call to setXY discards its third argument and collapses Saturn’s ring to a line. The moving belt and Bloom work; the composer has no OutputPass and applies ACES only partially. Atmospheres are rim glows. There are no moons or comets. Spins are random and ignore the simulation multiplier. There is no pause control; R only restores the camera. Focus and follow only steer the look-at target. Half-float postprocessing has no fallback or scene MSAA. Actual UnrealBloomPass output tone-maps the base image through MeshBasicMaterial, then adds Bloom without mapping the combined result; ACES receives0.4 partial credit.",
