    'MiMo2.6Flash(Unknown)V1-TasksAssignedByOpus5': {"title": "Real-Time Solar-System Model", note: "Rechecked final overrides against the task. Native offline WebGL2 provides Kepler motion and matching guides, eight task-prescribed moons, Halley, a moving belt, mutual ring shadows, Bloom, final ACES and analytic atmosphere. An inward-wound sphere with proper models and actual BACK/CCW culling is an independent integrity fault. An extra negative spin-matrix convention and fixed 30-hour moon spins remain data errors. Selecting a non-Earth planet assigns to a const in its info update, preventing the final focus-distance step; runtime and focus are partial, without a core-loop fatal finding. Drag does not suppress click and computed minimum zoom distance is not enforced. Tracking and pause/Now/reverse work. Prompt-inherent signed-spin and moon contradictions are exempt.", "issue": "Selecting a non-Earth planet repeatedly throws Assignment to constant variable, breaking information updates and automatic close-up zoom."},
    'MiMo2.6Pro(Unknown)V1': {"title": "MiMo Solar System · Keplerian Model", "note": "Networked Three.js has fixed real elements, Kepler motion and matching guides, a moving belt, Bloom and ACES through the final OutputPass. Rings lack mutual shadows and atmosphere is rim glow. All six moons have the opposite orbital mapping to the planets; their invalidity is charged only to moons. Wall-clock spin, signed rotation with large tilt and a perihelion-only speed readout remain independent data faults. Pointer-down selects while dragging, minimum zoom can enter the Sun and focus interpolation terminates early. Camera and target translations implement continuous follow. Pause leaves physical spin running and System View is not a full reset. The unsupported old integrity deduction is removed. No comets or confirmed fatal fault."},
