    'Grok4.7(xhigh)V1': {"title": "Solar System", "note": "Native offline long-range JPL/Kepler motion and matching guides, a moving belt, world-space mutual ring shadows, Bloom/final ACES, Halley and an independently moving Encke are effective; atmosphere is rim glow. Of thirteen moons, the Moon and Titania retain credit; the others have actual Jupiter-basis or directed-equatorial errors. Pluto uses negative spin with an IAU north pole, an independent data fault. Sphere winding is explicitly corrected and depth writes are restored after transparency, excluding the 0910 culling/clear faults. Minimum zoom lacks body protection and pause lacks a full A reset. At the default 3 days/s, Phobos remains off-screen in all twelve samples after focus distance settles within 2% of its goal. Target low-pass lag therefore receives partial follow credit, without another focus or zoom deduction."},
    'Grok4.7(xhigh)V1-TasksAssignedByOpus5': {"title": "Real-Time Solar-System Model", note: "Final bindings were rechecked against the full task. Native offline WebGL2 implements JPL rates/Kepler motion and matching planet, moon and Halley paths, eight task-algorithm moons, a moving belt, mutual ring shadows, Bloom/final ACES and analytic atmosphere. Sphere winding is corrected and model, normal and inverse-light matrices include current spin. Drag, complete focus/continuous follow and physical pause/Now/reverse work. Minimum zoom .45 is below the Sun radius 4.6 without a radius guard, retaining partial zoom. Prescribed signed spin, moon-algorithm and Halley-date contradictions are exempt; no full reset is required. No extra comets or independent data/integrity fault was found."},
    'MiniMaxM3.1FlashPreview(Max)V1': {"title": "Solar-System Motion Model", "note": "Native offline WebGL2 provides JPL/Kepler motion, a Meeus Moon, moving belts, mutual ring shadows, Bloom/final ACES and safe zoom; atmosphere is rim glow. Iapetus at 15.47° to the drawn equator regains basic credit; five Uranian moons retain direction errors, leaving fifteen valid moons with unchanged capped bonuses. Newly verified moon guides omit actual inclination/node and force the parent equator, so path fit is partial. Independent data faults include the obliquity-transform sign, a full lunar offset added to EMB and eccentric anomaly used as true anomaly. A timer adds permanent RAF chains, measured growing from 38 to 89. Its 8ms guard keeps paused JD/spin fixed; runtime is 4, without claiming clock acceleration or an observed L2 failure. Separate cross-LOD index-count mismatches produce actual GL1282 errors, retaining integrity 3.5. Focus changes target until double-clicked; direct tracking and physical pause work, with no full A reset."},
    'MiniMaxM3.1FlashPreview(Max)V1-TasksAssignedByOpus5': {"title": "Solar System · Real-Time Orbital Model", note: "Native offline WebGL2 implements JPL/Kepler motion, eight task-algorithm moons, Halley, moving belts, Bloom/final ACES and analytic atmosphere. Newly verified ring-on-body shading multiplies a world light vector by the normal matrix R/r instead of inverse R and is one-sided; ring-side planet shadow remains correct, so rings are partial. Added dwarf spin units multiply hours by 24 and explanatory resonance counts are incorrect, retaining data 4.5. Sphere/model winding, normal matrices and depth state are sound. Drag, focus, tracking and task pause/Now/reverse work; a .35 zoom minimum lacks body protection. Prompt-prescribed spin/moon/date contradictions are exempt. An additional numerical check resolves the previously pending guide test: 512 uniform-M Halley samples leave a 6.53071-unit nearest-chord gap near the reachable 1986 perihelion, exceeding the 0.34 nucleus radius. Path fit is partial while other guides remain valid; no duplicate data or Halley deduction is applied."},
    'GPT6.1Sol(Ultra)V1': {"title": "ORRERY · Dynamic Solar-System Observatory", "note": "The complete final source was rechecked. Offline native WebGL2 implements JPL rates/Kepler motion and matching guides, thirteen moons with valid basic directed frames, Halley, moving belts, mutual ring shadows, HDR/Bloom/final ACES and eight-step optical-depth atmosphere scattering. Mean moon elements, illustrative initial phases, EMB position and Halley two-body approximations are disclosed; no independent fault supports requiring extra high-precision ephemerides. Old data 4 and integrity 4.5 are restored to 5. Outward winding, proper models, depth state and scale transitions are sound. Drag, radius-protected zoom, complete focus and direct tracking work. Physical pause works; Now and Overview remain separate without a full A reset. An additional numerical check resolves the previously pending guide test: 512 uniform-M Halley samples leave a 0.32834-unit nearest-chord gap near the reachable 1986 perihelion, exceeding the 0.09 nucleus radius. Path fit is partial while other guides remain valid; no duplicate data or Halley deduction is applied."},
    'GPT6Astra(Max)V1': { title: 'ORRERY · Dynamic Solar-System Observatory', note: "The complete embedded Three app and final RAF/events retain all inputs. Current JPL/Kepler positions share uniform-E640 paths. The single Moon uses an independent5.145° ecliptic orbit with node/apsis motion and correct directed period; its128-point translated line refreshes every20days with sub-nucleus error. Two-way Saturn shadows correctly invert the axis and spin,2500 moving asteroids execute, HalfFloat scene MSAA is real and bloom is followed by explicit ACES. Atmosphere remains rim-only. IAU north poles with signed spin periods avoid duplicate tilt reversal. Following uses exact translations and close-view bounds are safe, but true-scale overview minimum.025 penetrates Sun.03723765 (partial zoom). Physical pause works; date and camera restore separately for A. No Halley or extra comet exists.", tags: ['in Codex', 'Offline textures · 1 moon · no comets'] },
